---@field OriginKeepaliveTimeout? aws.cloudfront.integer Specifies how long, in seconds, CloudFront persists its connection to the origin. The minimum timeout is 1 second, the maximum is 120 seconds, and the default (if you don't specify otherwise) is 5 seconds.
---@field IpAddressType? aws.cloudfront.IpAddressType|string Specifies which IP protocol CloudFront uses when connecting to your origin. If your origin uses both IPv4 and IPv6 protocols, you can choose dualstack to help optimize reliability.
